Consumer complaint narrative:
b'I submitted complaint regarding my federal student loan account(s) currently or formerly serviced by Aidvantage, concerning:
	Unverified and potentially invalid loan balances;
	Failure to provide required legal documentation of indebtedness;
	Inaccurate credit reporting; and
	Violations of federal privacy protections.
I have formally requested that the servicer provide:
	A signed Master Promissory Note (MPN);
	A full chain of assignment or ownership from the Department of Education to the current servicer;
	A complete payment history and balance breakdown.

Disputed Accounts:XXXXAccount Number\XXXX am also gravely concerned about the improper and unauthorized disclosure of my personal loan data, particularly in light of recent revelations involving the Department of Educations breach and the Default Oversight Group and Evaluation (DOGE). As reported, data was accessed or shared with third parties without borrower consent, possibly violating both the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA, 20 U.S.C.  1232g) and the Privacy Act of 1974 (5 U.S.C.  552a).
I have not received any notification that my data was shared or exposed, nor was I given an opportunity to opt out or consent to the release of sensitive financial information to federal contractors or third parties.

What I Am Requesting from the CFPB:
	A full investigation into the loan servicers failure to validate and substantiate the debt;
	Immediate correction or deletion of the inaccurately reported loan from all major credit bureaus;
	Confirmation that any unauthorized disclosures of my loan information are investigated, disclosed to me, and remediated in accordance with privacy law;
	Potential enforcement action against the loan servicer or Department of Education contractors who may be mishandling borrower data and violating federal regulations.'

